igure 11: A visual summary of DeepSeek V3.2=E2=80=99s Sparse Attention mech=
anism.</figcaption></figure></div><p></p><p></p><p>To sum it up, the indexe=
r and token selector result in each token attending to a few past tokens th=
at the model has learned to consider most relevant, rather than all tokens =
or a fixed local window.</p><p>The goal here was not to improve the perform=
ance over DeepSeek V3.1-Terminus but to reduce the performance degradation =
(due to the sparse attention mechanism) while benefiting from improved effi=
ciency.</p><p><span>Overall, the DSA reduces the computational complexity o=
f the attention mechanism from quadratic O(=F0=9D=90=BF</span><sup>2</sup><=
span>), where L is the sequence length, to a linear O(=F0=9D=90=BF=F0=9D=91=
=98), where =F0=9D=91=98 (=E2=89=AA=F0=9D=90=BF) is the number of selected =
tokens.</span></p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post"><strong>5. DeepSeekMath =
V2 with Self-Verification and Self-Refinement</strong><div class=3D"pencraf=
