f the verifier=E2=80=99s proof analyses =E2=80=93 as evaluated by the meta-=
verifier =E2=80=93 improved from 0.85 to 0.96, while maintaining the same a=
ccuracy in proof score prediction.</p></blockquote><p>This is actually quit=
e an interesting setup. If you are familiar with generative adversarial net=
works (GANs), you may see the analogy here. For instance, the proof verifie=
r (think of it as a GAN discriminator) improves the proof generator, and th=
e proof generator generates better proofs, further pushing the proof verifi=
er.</p><p>The meta score is used during training of the verifier (LLM 2) an=
d the generator (LLM 1). It is not used at inference time in the self=E2=80=
